      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could consider having a framework in `vmbase` for clients to register their handlers, which `MemoryTracker` could use internally. One option is to define a static in `vmbase/exception.rs` storing a reference to an `ExceptionHandler` trait, and move the code there as a default implementation of the trait. Clients could customize the trait as needed and register an implementation at the beginning of execution. Does this align with what you want?\n\nHowever, I think that the current approach is simpler and more straightforward than introducing another static variable to the code.",
